intuition:
You have a table of customers and a table of orders. Not every customer has placed an order. If you want to see all customers and their orders, use a LEFT JOIN on customers. Customers with no orders still show up, but the order columns are NULL. If you want only customers who've actually ordered, use INNER JOIN and the non-buyers disappear from the result.

The mental model: LEFT JOIN is 'give me everything on the left, attach whatever matches from the right'. INNER JOIN is 'only give me the rows where both sides agreed to show up'.

